{
  "compileOnSave": false,
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "./dist/out-tsc",
    // WHY THERE IS NO baseUrl HERE
    //
    // The obvious way to write these aliases is `baseUrl: "./src/app"` with
    // `"@core/*": ["core/*"]`, and it is worse. Setting baseUrl switches on
    // non-relative module resolution for the WHOLE project, not just for these
    // four patterns. From then on a typo that drops the `@` -- `from
    // 'core/models/order.model'` -- stops being a compile error and starts
    // quietly resolving to a real file. A refactor that made a misspelled
    // import compile is a refactor that can hide a broken one.
    //
    // TypeScript resolves `paths` entries relative to the tsconfig that declares
    // them when baseUrl is absent, so spelling the `src/app/` prefix out in each
    // pattern gets the same result with none of that blast radius. The `./`
    // leading slash on each value is required, not stylistic: without baseUrl,
    // TS5090 rejects a bare `src/app/core/*` as a non-relative path and tells
    // you so. The cost is that the prefix is repeated four times; the benefit is
    // that a wrong import is still a wrong import.
    //
    // WHY THIS IS THE ROOT tsconfig AND NOT tsconfig.app.json
    // The root is what tsx resolves when `npm run test:logic` loads tests/*.ts,
    // and those files import from core/. Aliases declared only in
    // tsconfig.app.json would leave the test suite unable to resolve them.
    //
    // WHY @env/ EXISTS
    // It is the only alias that points outside src/app, and it exists because
    // app.config.ts otherwise needed `../environments/environment` -- the single
    // ugliest import path in the codebase. Worth an alias precisely because it
    // is a one-off.
    //
    // NO angular.json CHANGE IS NEEDED. The `application` builder honours
    // TypeScript `paths` natively. The `paths` alias object under the old
    // `webpack` builder was a separate, deprecated mechanism; adding one would
    // mean configuring resolution twice and having them disagree.
    "paths": {
      "@core/*": ["./src/app/core/*"],
      "@shared/*": ["./src/app/shared/*"],
      "@features/*": ["./src/app/features/*"],
      "@env/*": ["./src/environments/*"]
    },
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    // Turned on deliberately, as its own commit, because the gap analysis had
    // this standing as a "known gap": dead code in this project was only ever
    // found by reading it, so the next batch would have been too.
    //
    // What it caught on the first pass, all in files whose dead paths had been
    // commented at length as if they were live:
    //   - VoucherService's doc/updateDoc/increment imports, orphaned when
    //     recordRedemption moved into reconcileOrderStock.
    //   - getPricingForSet in OrderService, orphaned when the PRICING_MATRIX
    //     checkout fallback was removed so the client fails closed like the
    //     server does.
    //   - the Subscription field and rxjs import on AnalyticsPage, orphaned when
    //     its onSnapshot read became a paged getDocs walk.
    //
    // Expect a burst of failures the first time this is enabled in a project;
    // that is the point. `noUnusedParameters` is deliberately NOT set -- an
    // intentionally-unused parameter (an event handler signature, an injected
    // dependency kept for symmetry) is not a defect, and flagging those would
    // train people to ignore the compiler.
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "importHelpers": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "useDefineForClassFields": false,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "dom"]
  },
  "angularCompilerOptions": {
    "enableI18nLegacyMessageIdFormat": false,
    "strictInjectionParameters": true,
    "strictInputAccessModifiers": true,
    "strictTemplates": true
  }
}
